#### EqualityComparer<T>.Create

To create an equality comparer from a key selector function, use the new [EqualityComparer<T>.Create](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.collections.generic.equalitycomparer-1.create) factory method. You can pass an optional [IEqualityComparer<T>](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.collections.generic.iequalitycomparer-1) for the key type itself:

```

// Create an equality comparer based on a key selector
var byName = EqualityComparer<(string Name, int Age)>.Create(p => p.Name);

var people = new HashSet<(string Name, int Age)>(byName)
{
    ("Alice", 30),
    ("Bob", 25),
    ("Alice", 40), // Duplicate by name — not added
};
Console.WriteLine(people.Count); // 2
```

